# Local state. It records every resource ID in the stack and, for some providers, secrets in
# plaintext -- it is not committable, and this stack's state is worthless after teardown anyway.
# The production answer is an S3 backend with DynamoDB locking; see versions.tf for why that is
# deliberately not set up here.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
crash.log

# Saved plan files. Binary, machine- and moment-specific, and they embed resolved values from
# state -- a committed plan is stale the instant anything changes and is not reviewable anyway.
tfplan
*.tfplan
*.tfvars
!example.tfvars
